{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962349,"nonce":"msYBnFg5e9rCIMj6G+/wVnsi5tA=","title":"TextContent and FontFamily bindings apply nothing","message":"hl_blinc_apply_string (blinc_abi/src/layout_router.rs) accepts these\nproperties and applies nothing: Blinc has no way to change a text node's\nTextMeasureContext after creation (blinc 248dc9b7219b94880ae2095260ec026c686c8b69c03b32df6702584b4e862164).\nThis is the spec's headline case, `\u003ctext\u003eValue: ${count}\u003c/text\u003e`.\n\nOnce Blinc has LayoutTree::update_text:\n- Blinc's queue only carries render and layout writes, so a text binding's\n  render closure records the new value per node, and Tree::flush applies the\n  recorded text writes through update_text before compute_layout.\n- FontSize on a text node must reach TextMeasureContext.font_size too, or the\n  node is drawn at one size and measured at another (today it only sets\n  RenderProps.font_size).\n- Smoke test: bind a Text's content to a computed string and check its width\n  follows the signal.","files":null}]}